# Deliberately empty: there is NO catch-all rule here.
#
# This deployment is a Worker with an assets binding (see wrangler.jsonc), and
# worker/index.ts already performs the SPA fallback to _shell.html. It does so
# conditionally — only for navigation requests, and only after the asset server
# has answered 404.
#
# A `/*  /_shell.html  200` rule here is not a second opinion, it is a veto: the
# asset server applies _redirects before matching files, so the catch-all
# matched /assets/*.js, /theme-init.js, /manifest.webmanifest and every other
# real file and answered each one with the HTML shell. The browser then refused
# them all on MIME grounds ("Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the
# server responded with a MIME type of text/html") and nothing on the page
# booted. Do not reintroduce it while worker/index.ts is the entry point.
#
# If this app is ever deployed to Pages instead — no Worker, no fallback — the
# rule below is what it needs, and it is safe there because nothing else does
# the job:
#
#   /*    /_shell.html   200
#
# Note _shell.html, not index.html: TanStack Start's SPA mode (spa.enabled in
# vite.config.ts) emits no index.html at all.
